uence overall.\nThe results suggest that demographic factors, particularly age, are more predictive of appointment adherence than individual clinical conditions in this dataset.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## How does wait time between scheduling and appointment date affect no-show probability?","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Do patients who receive reminders (SMS or not) show different no-show behavior across age groups?","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Among patients witht similar demographics, do certain \"visit note themes\" correlate with higher no-show rates?","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### What proportion of patients miss their first appointment, and how does that relate to future attendance behavior?","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"","metadata":{"trusted":true},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null}]}